cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "TRF: Tri-Lateral Retention Feasibility Model — executable artefact"
type: software
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-10-31
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Abbasia
    given-names: Arshad Akhtar
    affiliation: "Høgskolen i Molde (Molde University College)"
    email: arshad.a.abbasia@himolde.no
repository-code: "https://github.com/Astheno-sphere/TRF"
url: "https://trfhimolde.streamlit.app/"
abstract: >-
  Executable artefact for the MSc thesis "Verifiable Crypto-Erasure for
  Cross-Border Health Data Audit Trails under the European Health Data Space"
  (Høgskolen i Molde, 2026). A constraint checker for the Tri-Lateral
  Retention Feasibility (TRF) Model over 200 synthetic records (seed
  20260915), with an exhaustive cross-check, a bounded Z3 SMT check, a
  Synthea FHIR R4 realism layer, a cryptographic envelope module and a
  Streamlit viewer. Results are checked on generated data; key destruction
  is simulated and treated as attested, not proven.
keywords:
  - European Health Data Space
  - GDPR Article 17
  - cryptographic erasure
  - audit trail
  - data retention
  - constraint satisfaction
  - design science research
